{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06NQ", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d6f490743f7550ed4df3028ff79916b3a3023c2eb67ce4345a22d5f78fd9ee5a", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe following type of lemma is occasionally useful.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:42ae01a96a85cd387aadca3e9854aee81ca6bfdb2e5578f26f3daf59626c4e7a", "unit_id": "tag:06NQ:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06NQ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$X \\to Y \\to Z$", "MATH_0003": "$P$", "MATH_0004": "$S$", "MATH_0005": "$X \\to Z$", "MATH_0006": "$P$", "MATH_0007": "$X \\to Y$", "MATH_0008": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0009": "$Y \\to Z$", "MATH_0010": "$P$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-curiosity}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9b78139f64f5a5c85d3e90d9cc0825402c61027b709b71f10abfd2e464cea9fd", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:769b6aaac55061389a95f5f5243ebd6a00f3745db912a98a9b586352e150b22e", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be morphism of algebraic spaces.\nLet <MATH_0003> be one of the following properties of morphisms of algebraic spaces\nover <MATH_0004>:\nflat, locally finite type, locally finite presentation.\nAssume that <MATH_0005> has <MATH_0006> and that\n<MATH_0007> is a surjection of sheaves on <MATH_0008>.\nThen <MATH_0009> is <MATH_0010>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d694f740dd27e9dc8be65bc70dacf2a46bbefb5d53b894bd56b7dc3ab858c461", "unit_id": "tag:06NR:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06NQ", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0003": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0004": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$W$", "MATH_0002": "$W \\to Z$", "MATH_0003": "$V$", "MATH_0004": "$V \\to W \\times_Z Y$", "MATH_0005": "$U$", "MATH_0006": "$U \\to V \\times_Y X$", "MATH_0007": "$\\{V_i \\to V\\}$", "MATH_0008": "$V_i \\to X$", "MATH_0009": "$V_i \\to Y$", "MATH_0010": "$U \\to X$", "MATH_0011": "$\\{V_i \\times_X U \\to V\\}$", "MATH_0012": "$U$", "MATH_0013": "$U \\to V$", "MATH_0014": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0015": "$P$", "MATH_0016": "$U \\to W$", "MATH_0017": "$P$", "MATH_0018": "$V \\to W$", "MATH_0019": "$P$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-definition-flat}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-definition-locally-finite-type}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-definition-locally-finite-presentation}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{descent-lemma-curiosity}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9952ea382d2db052011fafcf45706de40b7077c3ca2a466b3ec73be88683295c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:60b6ef7cfc54b7e0a373d3e1d772b9b5da9fb280fae67eea594b55004333c313", "source_text": "Choose a scheme <MATH_0001> and a surjective <ACCENT_0001>tale morphism <MATH_0002>.\nChoose a scheme <MATH_0003> and a surjective <ACCENT_0002>tale morphism <MATH_0004>.\nChoose a scheme <MATH_0005> and a surjective <ACCENT_0003>tale morphism <MATH_0006>.\nBy assumption we can find an fppf covering <MATH_0007> and\nlifts <MATH_0008> of the morphism <MATH_0009>. Since <MATH_0010> is surjective\n<ACCENT_0004>tale we see that over the members of the fppf covering\n<MATH_0011> we have lifts into <MATH_0012>. Hence <MATH_0013> induces\na surjection of sheaves on <MATH_0014>.\nBy our definition of what it means to have property <MATH_0015> for a\nmorphism of algebraic spaces (see\nMorphisms of Spaces,\nDefinition <REF_0001>,\nDefinition <REF_0002>, and\nDefinition <REF_0003>)\nwe see that <MATH_0016> has <MATH_0017> and we have to show <MATH_0018> has <MATH_0019>.\nThus we reduce the question to the case of morphisms of schemes\nwhich is treated in\nDescent, Lemma <REF_0004>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7d8d9e1d3ded097c3a6b1ed097d1b52c0048805edd3d595ce6772691b90df285", "unit_id": "tag:06NR:proof"}
